## The Lab Advantage

At 1.5 carats, The Lab Advantage is the most important concept in asscher cut buying. Understanding it changes how you shop.

A natural 1.5ct asscher VS1 costs $12,000–18,000 for the stone alone. A lab 1.52ct D-IF costs $2,795. The carat weight is the same.

The clarity is better in the lab stone. The color is better in the lab stone. The certification is from IGI, which is the standard for lab asscher grading.

The difference is not quality — it is origin and resale behavior. Lab diamonds do not hold resale value the way natural diamonds do.

If long-term resale or certified natural origin matters to you, natural is the choice. If you want the best possible stone at 1.5ct for your ring budget, lab wins at this size category with no contest.

The practical application: if your total ring budget is $5,000, you cannot buy a natural 1.5ct asscher. You can buy an outstanding lab 1.52ct D-IF with an Art Deco setting and have $1,015 left over.

> "At 1.5ct, the lab option is not a backup plan — it is the correct choice for 90% of buyers in this category. The stone is better-graded than most natural alternatives buyers could afford. D-IF is the highest possible grade. The asscher's step facets show you exactly how clean that clarity is every time you look at the ring. No buyer who has seen a D-IF step cut in person has questioned the choice." — Farzana Hasan, **[Diamond Critics](https://diamondcritics.com/about-farzana/)**

