**Verdict:** The natural asscher option at the 1.5ct quality level starts at $8,141 for a complete ring — with a GIA E-VVS1 stone that meets every grade requirement. This is the right choice for buyers who need certified natural provenance and are comfortable with the premium. For buyers whose priority is carat weight and clarity, lab delivers more stone for significantly less.

### What to Check on a Natural Asscher Cut GIA Certificate

When buying any natural asscher cut, the GIA certificate is not the whole story. Request the inclusion plot alongside the certificate.

Check three things on that plot: inclusion position (VS1 inclusions should be near the girdle edge, not the table center), table percentage (58–65% is ideal for asscher cuts), and polish and symmetry grades (Excellent or Very Good only at this price level).

At 1.5ct, inclusions that sit under the table are amplified by the step-facet reflections more than at smaller sizes. An inclusion at the 6 o'clock girdle position in a 1.5ct asscher is essentially invisible face-up. The same inclusion at the center of the table is visible even at VS1.

Always request the video alongside the GIA certificate for any natural 1.5ct asscher. Buying on grades alone without a face-up video at this size is an expensive mistake that the certificate alone will not protect you from.

> "Natural 1.5ct asscher buyers are a specific type. They want GIA. They want provenance. They are not comparing to lab pricing — they already know lab is the budget option. I respect that choice completely. The E-VVS1 at $7,281 is a beautiful stone. You will not find an inclusion in it face-up at any viewing angle. The windmill pattern is deep and perfectly centered." — Farzana Hasan, **[Diamond Critics](https://diamondcritics.com/about-farzana/)**

