e Gold</td><td>Excellent — clean prong holds octagonal outline</td><td>Most modern, lowest price, stone-forward design</td></tr><tr><td>#4</td><td><a href="https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings/design-your-own-ring/petite-hidden-halo-solitaire-plus-diamond-engagement-ring-in-14k-yellow-gold-item-192506?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational">Petite Hidden Halo YG</a></td><td><a href="https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings/design-your-own-ring/petite-hidden-halo-solitaire-plus-diamond-engagement-ring-in-14k-yellow-gold-item-192506?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational">$1,255</a></td><td>14k Yellow Gold</td><td>Good — halo sits below table, outline preserved</td><td>Extra sparkle under the stone, clean face-up profile</td></tr><tr><td>#5</td><td><a href="https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings/design-your-own-ring/art-deco-inspired-fleur-de-lis-pave-vintage-style-engagement-ring-in-14k-rose-gold-by-james-allen-item-315297?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational">Art Deco Fleur-De-Lis RG</a></td><td><a href="https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings/design-your-own-ring/art-deco-inspired-fleur-de-lis-pave-vintage-style-engagement-ring-in-14k-rose-gold-by-james-allen-item-315297?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational">$1,190</a></td><td>14k Rose Gold</td><td>Excellent — rose gold softens geometric edges</td><td>Romantic vintage look, same Art Deco detail, warm metal</td></tr></tbody></table>

**Verdict:** The Art Deco Fleur-De-Lis ranks #1 at every asscher carat size. At 1.5ct the case is even stronger — the larger stone fills the Art Deco basket more dramatically. The Ten Prong Solitaire is the right choice if you want the stone to lead and the setting to disappear.

[![Asscher cut diamond ring yellow gold full halo round diamond pavé band engagement ring](/images/asscher-cut-diamond-ring-yellow-gold-halo-pave-band.jpg)](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings/asscher-cut-diamond-rings?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational)

### Solitaire Settings for 1.5ct

The [Ten Prong Solitaire in white gold at $860](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings/design-your-own-ring/ten-prong-solitaire-engagement-ring-in-14k-white-gold-by-james-allen-item-311235?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) is the best entry setting for any asscher cut stone. The ten prongs are positioned at the eight corners of the octagonal girdle — holding the stone cleanly without obscuring the step-cut outline from above.

At 1.5ct, the solitaire lets the stone do the visual work. The IGI 1.52ct D-IF asscher in a clean white gold solitaire is a complete, finished ring for $3,655. The stone has enough presence at this size that no additional setting detail is needed.

Yellow gold solitaire versions are available at the same $860 — [yellow gold here](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings/design-your-own-ring/ten-prong-solitaire-engagement-ring-in-14k-yellow-gold-by-james-allen-item-311236?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) and [rose gold here](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings/design-your-own-ring/ten-prong-solitaire-engagement-ring-in-14k-rose-gold-by-james-allen-item-311237?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational).

One note on prong placement: at 1.5ct the asscher's corners are larger and more prominent. The ten-prong design grips all eight girdle corners evenly.

This matters practically — a six-prong round setting adapted for an asscher is not the same. The corner prongs protect the most vulnerable points of the octagonal outline, which chips more easily than a round stone's continuous girdle.

### Art Deco Settings for 1.5ct

The [Art Deco Fleur-De-Lis in white gold at $1,190](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings/design-your-own-ring/art-deco-inspired-fleur-de-lis-pave-vintage-style-engagement-ring-in-14k-white-gold-by-james-allen-item-315298?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) is the natural home of the asscher cut at any size.

At 1.5ct, the pavé shoulders and Art Deco detail frame the stone's larger presence without competing with it. The square basket is designed to hold a square step-cut stone. The result is a ring that looks entirely intentional — as if the setting was created specifically for the asscher's shape and the 1920s era that made it famous.

The [rose gold version at $1,190](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings/design-your-own-ring/art-deco-inspired-fleur-de-lis-pave-vintage-style-engagement-ring-in-14k-rose-gold-by-james-allen-item-315297?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) softens the geometric outline with warm metal. Paired with the [IGI 1.52ct D-IF at $2,795](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/27991043?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational), the total ring is $3,985.

### Cathedral Settings for 1.5ct

The [Tapered Cathedral Solitaire in yellow gold at $1,240](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings/design-your-own-ring/tapered-cathedral-solitaire-engagement-ring-in-14k-yellow-gold-item-203288?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) is the formal option in this setting group. The arched cathedral design elevates the stone above the finger on two tapered rails, creating a profile that is taller and more dramatic than a flat solitaire.

At 1.5ct, the elevated profile draws attention to the asscher's face-up geometry. Looking down at the ring, the octagonal outline and windmill pattern are fully visible with no shoulder pavé to distract. This is a ring for buyers who want the stone to read clean and architectural.

The cathedral arch is historically accurate for the asscher's 1920s Art Deco period. The combination of a yellow gold cathedral setting and an asscher cut stone is a period-correct pairing — the style the stone was originally designed to occupy.

