## Expert Summary

The 1.5 carat asscher cut diamond ring is the size where lab wins clearly and natural buyers need to understand the premium they are paying.

Lab delivers 1.52ct D-IF for $2,795. The Total Ring Number starts at $3,655 and reaches $4,815 with the 1.84ct step-up in an Art Deco setting. Every stone meets The Clarity Floor at the highest possible grade.

Natural 1.5ct asschers require a $12,000+ stone budget. The GIA E-VVS1 configuration in this guide starts at $8,141 for a complete ring — using the closest available certified natural asscher from current market inventory.

The 3 price mistakes all point to the same outcome: buyers who skip The Lab Advantage at this size, underestimate the setting cost, or buy below G color end up with a ring that cost more and delivered less than it should. All three are avoidable with the information in this guide.

Full asscher cut resources — including size comparisons, certification guidance, and setting rankings for every asscher carat weight — at the [asscher cut diamond guide](/asscher-cut-diamond).

