**Buy the entry lab ring ($3,655)** if: You want 1.52ct D-IF asscher, the best possible grades at 1.5ct size, and the lowest total. Pair the [IGI 1.52ct D-IF at $2,795](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/27991043?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) with the [Ten Prong Solitaire WG at $860](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings/design-your-own-ring/ten-prong-solitaire-engagement-ring-in-14k-white-gold-by-james-allen-item-311235?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational). Total: **$3,655.**

**Buy the Art Deco lab ring ($3,985)** if: You want the full asscher experience — 1.52ct D-IF step cut in the setting the shape was designed for. Pair the [IGI 1.52ct D-IF at $2,795](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/27991043?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) with the [Art Deco Fleur-De-Lis WG at $1,190](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings/design-your-own-ring/art-deco-inspired-fleur-de-lis-pave-vintage-style-engagement-ring-in-14k-white-gold-by-james-allen-item-315298?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational). Total: **$3,985.**

**Buy the premium lab ring ($4,815)** if: You want noticeably more stone than the 1.52ct entry — 1.84ct D-IF is a visible upgrade in face-up size. Pair the [IGI 1.84ct D-IF at $3,625](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/28929410?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) with the [Art Deco Fleur WG at $1,190](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings/design-your-own-ring/art-deco-inspired-fleur-de-lis-pave-vintage-style-engagement-ring-in-14k-white-gold-by-james-allen-item-315298?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational). Total: **$4,815.**

**Buy the natural ring ($8,141+)** if: Certified GIA provenance is non-negotiable and you have the stone budget. Pair the [GIA 1.05ct E-VVS1 at $7,281](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/16991197?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) with your preferred setting. True 1.5ct natural asschers start at $12,000+ for the stone alone.

No matter which option you choose, apply The Clarity Floor before you finalize. VS1 minimum at 1.5ct is not a guideline — it is the line between a ring you will love and one you will notice every time you look at it in direct light.

The asscher cut rewards buyers who understand its specific requirements. Every rule in this guide exists because the step-cut geometry exposes what a brilliant cut hides.

Follow the rules, and the 1.5 carat asscher cut diamond ring is one of the most striking rings available at any price point. See the full category guide at [Asscher Cut Diamond](/asscher-cut-diamond).

